all pieces of French patisserie consisting of small spheres of choux pastry, sugared and baked. The term was known in the 16th century, and was originally applied to small savoury spheres. Since the late 17th century chouquettes have been sweet."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-chouquette"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chouquette"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Profiterole","dish/profiterole"]]],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine",[["Profiterole","dish/profiterole"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Choux pastry","ingredient/choux-pastry"],["Custard","ingredient/custard"],["Ganache","ingredient/ganache"],["Ice cream","ingredient/ice-cream"],["Vanilla ice cream","ingredient/vanilla-ice-cream"],["Whipped cream","ingredient/whipped-cream"]]}]},"dish/tarhonya":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/tarhonya","n":"Tarhonya","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 3 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Tarhonya or tarhoňa (Slovak: [ˈtarɦɔɲa]) is a dried egg- and wheat-based ingredient found in Hungarian and Slovak cuisine."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tarhonya"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarhonya"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Austrian cuisine","cuisine/austrian-cuisine"],["Hungarian cuisine","cuisine/hungarian-cuisine"],["Slovak cuisine","cuisine/slovak-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Vienna Sunday Kitchen","ref":"site/vienna-sunday-kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"vienna-sunday.kitchen","note":"Viennese food blog of Austrian home cooking and pastries, with English-language recipes.","url":"https://www.vienna-sunday.kitchen/newest-recipes/","suggested":true},{"name":"Lil Vienna","ref":"site/lilvienna-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lilvienna.com","note":"Austrian recipes from Ursula and David, two Austrians living in Boston.","url":"https://www.lilvienna.com/?p=1366","suggested":true},{"name":"Zsuzsa Is in the Kitchen","ref":"site/zsuzsaisinthekitchen-blogspot-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"zsuzsaisinthekitchen.blogspot.com","note":"Hungarian-born home cook's blog of traditional Hungarian recipes.","url":"https://zsuzsaisinthekitchen.blogspot.com/2010/01","suggested":true},{"name":"Slovak Cooking","ref":"site/slovakcooking-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"slovakcooking.com","note":"English-language site of Slovak home recipes started by a young Slovak cook.","url":"https://www.slovakcooking.com/about/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Austrian cuisine","links":[["Blini","dish/blini"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Chicken paprikash","dish/chicken-paprikash"],["Dampfnudel","dish/dampfnudel"],["Egg puffs and soup pearls","dish/egg-puffs-and-soup-pearls"],["Gulyásleves","dish/gulyasleves"],["Leberkäse","dish/leberkase"],["Liptauer","dish/liptauer"],["Pancake","dish/pancake"],["Potato salad","dish/potato-salad"],["Sachertorte","dish/sachertorte"],["Spätzle","dish/spatzle"],["Strudel","dish/strudel"],["Zopf","dish/zopf"]]}]},"dish/the-old-spaghetti-factory":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/the-old-spaghetti-factory","n":"The Old Spaghetti Factory","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["The Old Spaghetti Factory is an Italian-American-style chain restaurant in the United States, Canada, and Japan. The American restaurants are owned by OSF International, based in Portland, Oregon, while the Canadian restaurants are owned by The Old Spaghetti Factory Canada Ltd. In 2003, the U.S. company had sales of $105 million. As of 2024, the U.S. company has 43 restaurants in 13 states and Japan. The U.S. firm also operated an Old Spaghetti Factory in Hamburg, Germany, from 1983 to 1993, but this was its only European location."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-the-old-spaghetti-factory"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Old_Spaghetti_Factory"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","ref":"site/pastagrannies-substack-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","ref":"site/recipesfromitaly-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"recipesfromitaly.com","note":"Traditional Italian recipes written by Italian home cooks, organized by region and course.","url":"https://recipesfromitaly.com","suggested":true},{"name":"Manu's Menu","ref":"site/manusmenu-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"manusmenu.com","note":"Italian-born home cook Manuela sharing classic family and regional Italian dishes.","url":"https://www.manusmenu.com/about/about-this-site","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Italian cuisine","links":[["8½ Otto e Mezzo Bombana","dish/8-otto-e-mezzo-bombana"],["A16 (restaurant)","dish/a16-restaurant"],["Acquacotta","dish/acquacotta"],["Agliata","dish/agliata"],["Agnolotti","dish/agnolotti"],["Alfredo alla Scrofa","dish/alfredo-alla-scrofa"],["Alioto's","dish/alioto-s"],["Amalfi's Italian Restaurant","dish/amalfi-s-italian-restaurant"],["Amato's","dish/amato-s"],["Angelo's Civita Farnese","dish/angelo-s-civita-farnese"],["Antica Pizzeria Port'Alba","dish/antica-pizzeria-port-alba"],["Antico Pizza","dish/antico-pizza"],["Antipasto","dish/antipasto"],["Arancini","dish/arancini"],["ASK Italian","dish/ask-italian"],["Asti (restaurant)","dish/asti-restaurant"],["Ava Gene's","dish/ava-gene-s"],["Bamonte's","dish/bamon